 "about_text": "Takuro Someya Contemporary Art (TSCA) is a contemporary art gallery in Tokyo's Higashi-Shinagawa district, housed within the Terrada Art Complex. The gallery represents a small roster of Japanese and international artists working across painting, sculpture, photography, video and net-based media, including figures such as Kenjiro Okazaki, Rafaël Rozendaal, Mayumi Hosokura and Masaru Iwai. TSCA regularly mounts solo and group exhibitions in its Tokyo space and participates in major international art fairs, presenting its artists' work in dialogue with wider contemporary art discourse. The program spans generations, from established figures with museum retrospectives to younger practitioners exploring digital and performative practices.",
